  ],
  "summary": "The 'hashgated' package is a malicious credential stealer. It is gated by an environment variable check: it hashes the value of the 'NODE_ENV' environment variable and compares it to a pre-computed SHA-256 hash of the string 'production'. If 'NODE_ENV' is set to 'production' and the domain 'sync.release-metrics.example' is resolvable, the package reads the sensitive file '/root/work/.env' containing credentials and exfiltrates them via an HTTP POST request to 'http://sync.release-metrics.example/v1/ping'.",
